  "worked_solution": "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D\u2286{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $\u03c8(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that $F(x,y)=2xy\\,i+({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,j$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P(x,y)=2xy$ and $Q(x,y)={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}=2y,\\,\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y} & =2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a no stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}=2y+2y=4y\\ne 0.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
